  "question": {
    "text": "The kinetic energy of emitted electron is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> when the light incident on the metal has wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>. To double the kinetic energy, the incident light must have wavelength:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Using Einstein&#39;s photoelectric equation, kinetic energy of an electron is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math>&nbsp;when the incident wavelength is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>When kinetic energy doubles, then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Subtracting&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>, we have&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
